/* book: lead: A short pulse launched into a multimode fiber comes out longer, because its power is shared among many modes and each mode takes a different time to cross the fiber. This is intermodal (or modal) dispersion. It grows with length L and with the fractional index difference Δ, and it caps the bit rate of a multimode link. A graded-index core cuts it by a factor of about 8/Δ, eight hundred times at Δ  */
/* book Figure 2.5.1: In the step-index core (top) the steepest ray zig-zags at the critical angle and over 5 km falls 247 ns behind the axial ray. In the graded core (bottom) the off-axis ray curves back smoothly through faster, lower-index glass and falls behind by only 0.31 ns. */
