/* book Worked example 2: Q: For the same fiber (n₁ = 1.48, Δ = 0.01), find the RMS broadening per kilometre and the bandwidth–length product BTL from 0.2/σ, for the step-index and the optimum graded profile.
   1. Step index: σs = 1000 × 1.48 × 0.01 ÷ (2√3 × 3 × 10⁸) = 14.8 ÷ (1.039 × 10⁹) = 1.42 × 10⁻⁸ s = 14.2 ns per km.
   2. BTL = 0.2 ÷ 1.42 × 10⁻⁸ = 1.40 × 10⁷, so about 14 Mbit/s·km.
   3. Graded: σg = 1000 × 1.48 × 10⁻⁴ ÷ (20√3 × 3 × 10⁸) = 0.148 ÷ (1.039 × 10¹⁰) = 1.42 × 10⁻¹¹ s = 14.2 ps per km.
   4. BTL = 0.2 ÷ 1.42 × 10⁻¹¹ = 1.40 × 10¹⁰, so about 14 Gbit/s·km.
   Answer: σ = 14.2 ns/km and about 14 Mbit/s·km for step index; σ = 14.2 ps/km and about 14 Gbit/s·km for the optimum graded profile: the factor 10/Δ = 1000. */
