/* book exam traps: Using Δ = n₁ − n₂ instead of (n₁ − n₂)/n₁. For n₁ = 1.48 and n₂ = 1.465, Δ = 0.0101, not 0.015. | Taking L in km while c is in m/s. Put L in metres, or use the per-kilometre result 49.3 ns/km for n₁ = 1.48, Δ = 0.01. | Mixing the full spread and the RMS width. δT goes with B ≤ 1/(2δT); σ goes with B ≈ 0.2/σ. A rectangular spread has σ = δT/(2√3). | Writing the graded improvement as Δ. It is Δ/8 for the full spread and Δ/10 for the RMS width of the optimum profile. | Expecting intermodal dispersion in a single-mode fiber. With one mode there is no modal delay; its spread is chromatic or polarization mode dispersion. */
